meta {
  name: Trace one request end to end
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

get {
  url: {{host}}/audit-events?correlationId={{correlationId}}
  body: none
  auth: none
}

docs {
  200. Everything one request caused, across every entity it touched.

  This is the filter that turns the trail from a list into an explanation. To use it, send
  any write with an X-Correlation-Id header of your own - the API echoes it on every
  response and stamps it on every entry it produces - then ask for it back here.

  Run "Write under a correlation identifier" first and this returns exactly what that
  request caused. With no header supplied the API generates one, which is still on the
  response and still on the entries; it is only harder to guess afterwards.

  An empty result after a write that answered 409 is not a broken filter - it is the trail
  correctly recording that nothing happened. Refusals are logged, not audited.
}
